  |                                ^^^^^ expected one of none, linear

== a_fit_that_is_a_string
error[Z0403]: expected one of none, linear, found text
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:32
  |
2 | d.scatter(dose, response, fit: "linear")
  |                                ^^^^^^^^ a word, not a string
  |
  = help: write the word without quotes: `linear`

== a_line_through_categories_along_x
error[Z0401]: `fit: linear` of `scatter` fits a line of `y` on `x`, so `x` must be numbers, but `arm` is placed as categories
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:11
  |
2 | d.scatter(arm, response, fit: linear)
  |           ^^^ categories
  |                               ------ a line is asked for here
  |
  = help: a least-squares line needs a number along each axis; along `x` a date will do, and is counted in days. Leave `fit:` out for the points alone

== a_line_through_categories_along_y
