== a_value_below_nothing_on_a_log_axis
note: 1 row with NA in dose or response - 5 dropped (line 2)
error[Z0401]: `response - 5` has 2 values at or below 0, which have no place on a log scale: rows 1 and 2 of d
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:52
  |
2 | d.scatter(dose, response - 5, fit: linear).scale_y(log)
  |                                                    ^^^ the `y` axis is a log scale
  |
  = help: keep the rows with a value above 0, as in `where(response - 5 > 0)`; a square-root scale, `sqrt`, holds 0

== a_scatter_of_a_plot
error[Z0401]: `scatter` cannot be called on a Plot
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:1
  |
2 | d.plot(x: dose).scatter(dose, response)
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ this is a Plot
  |
  = help: `scatter` takes a Frame first; `x.scatter(...)` is `scatter(x, ...)`
